hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2187","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever sees something he dislikes in his leader (i.e., ruler or king), let him be patient, for whoever separates himself from the ruler even by a handspan will die the death of ignorance."" (Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas [may Allah be pleased with them both]) in another narration says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees something he dislikes in his ruler should be patient, for whoever separates from the congregation even by a handspan and then dies, he will die the death of ignorance."""
"2188","‘Sayyiduna ‘Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) called us, so we pledged allegiance to him. ‘Ubada (may Allah be pleased with him) says that during the pledge, the Prophet (peace be upon him) took this promise from us: that we would listen and obey his command in both happiness and sorrow, in hardship and ease, even if others are given preference over us without us deserving it (still we would be patient), and that we would not dispute with the rulers regarding authority, except (the Prophet, peace be upon him, says): “When you see open disbelief (disobedience) for which you have a clear proof from Allah.”"
"2189","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to say: ""The worst of creation are those people who will be alive when the Hour (Resurrection) comes."""
"2190","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): When complaints about the (evils) coming from Hajjaj were made to him (Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Be patient, for after this time, the era that will come upon you will be even worse than this. This will continue in this way until you meet your Lord. And I have heard (all) this from your Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2191","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""No Muslim should point a weapon at his (Muslim) brother (not even in jest), for he does not know, perhaps Satan may cause the weapon to go off from his hand, and (as a result of killing a Muslim) he may fall into a pit of Hell."""
"2192","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will soon be such tribulations in which the one who is sitting will be better than the one who is standing, and the one who is standing will be better than the one who is walking, and the one who is walking will be better than the one who is running. Whoever looks at them from afar, they will also involve him in that calamity. So whoever finds a refuge or a place of shelter should take refuge there."""
"2193","Narrated from Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he went to Hajjaj bin Yusuf. Hajjaj said to him, “O son of Akwa’! Have you turned back on your heels from the migration that you made to Madinah, that you are now going to the wilderness (leaving Madinah)?” He replied, “No, rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered me to live in the wilderness.”"
"2194","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah sends punishment upon a people, it befalls all the people of that community (whether they are righteous or wicked), and then they will be resurrected (on the Day of Judgment) according to their deeds."""
"2195","´Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` hypocrisy existed until the time of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (because Allah would inform him that such and such a person is a hypocrite), but in this era, a person is either a believer or a disbeliever (because the state of the heart is known to Allah; now matters are based on what is apparent)."
"2196","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until a fire emerges from Hijaz which will illuminate the necks of camels in Busra (i.e., the necks of camels will be visible in its light)."""
"2197","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Soon the Euphrates will uncover a treasure of gold. So whoever is present there should not take anything from it."""
"2198","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): Verily, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until two great groups fight each other, and there will be a severe battle between them, though their claim will be one and the same. And until about thirty liars (Dajjals) will appear, each of them claiming that he is the Messenger of Allah. And until knowledge will be taken away, and earthquakes will increase, and time will pass quickly, and tribulations will appear, and killing will increase, and wealth will become so abundant among you that it will flow like a flood, to the extent that a man will wish for someone to accept his charity, but when he offers it to someone, he will say, 'I have no need of it.' And (the Hour will not be established) until people compete in constructing high buildings, and until a man passes by a grave and says, 'Would that I were in his place (in the grave).' And until the sun rises from the west; then when it rises and people see it, they will all believe, but that will be the time when faith will not benefit anyone who did not believe before, or who did not do good deeds with his faith. And verily, the Hour will be established so suddenly that two men will have spread out a cloth between them for a transaction, but they will neither be able to complete the transaction nor fold it up (before the Hour is established). And verily, the Hour will be established so suddenly that a man will be carrying the milk of his she-camel, but will not be able to drink it (before the Hour is established). And a man will be repairing his water trough for his animals, but will not be able to water them (before the Hour is established). And verily, the Hour will be established so suddenly that a man will have raised a morsel to his mouth, but will not be able to eat it (before the Hour is established)."""
